{"zh":"锦绣布衣·丙","en":"Embroidered Cloth Robe - III"},"level":"0","description":{"zh":"采用了普通的面料并进行了纹饰处理的布衣，衣服的边缘处也添加了简单的纹饰。","en":"A cloth garment made of ordinary patterned fabric, with simple decorative trim added along the edges."},"defenceVal":"2","mp":"340","price":"1200","slot":{"zh":"护甲","en":"Armor"}},{"id":"WP1026805","name":{"zh":"绮陌冠","en":"Gallant Crown"},"level":"1","description":{"zh":"稍微简易些的小冠，多为朝中风流文士佩戴。","en":"A slightly simpler small crown, favored by the literary gentlemen of court."},"mp":"710","evade":"5","price":"3200","slot":{"zh":"头盔","en":"Helmet"}}],"family":{"children":{"label":{"zh":"子女","en":"Children"},"people":[{"id":"WJ1033415","code":"100"}]}},"clans":[{"id":"GI107815","name":{"zh":"东海缪氏","en":"The Miao Clan of Donghai"},"years":["0","999"],"desc":{"zh":"出自嬴姓，秦穆公谥号“缪”，子孙以谥为氏。西汉初兰陵缪生为申公弟子，官至长沙内史，开基立业。汉晋之际活跃于两淮的文学世家。缪袭历仕曹魏四世，官至尚书、光禄勋，有才学，多著述，曾奉诏作《魏鼓吹曲》十二首，参与编撰《皇览》，完成《昌言》。其孙缪播、缪胤于西晋末年为东海王司马越心腹。","en":"Originating from the Ying surname. Duke Mu of Qin was posthumously titled ‘Miu’, and his descendants took the posthumous name as their surname. In the early Western Han, Scholar Miu of Lanling, a disciple of Master Shen, rose to Chief Administrator of Changsha and founded the clan's fortunes. During the transition between Han and Jin, they were a literary Family prominent in the Huai River region. Miu Xi served across four reigns of Cao Wei, rising to Master of Writing and Minister of the Household. Renowned for his erudition and prolific writings, he composed twelve ‘Wei Drum-and-Pipe Songs’ by imperial decree, contributed to the compilation of the Imperial Overview, and completed Words of Prosperity. His grandsons Miu Bo and Miu Yin served as confidants of Sima Yue, Prince of Donghai, in the late Western Jin."},"talent":{"military":"1","commerce":"1","politics":"1"}}],"friendGroups":[],"body":{"name":"缪斐","height":"较矮","shape":"一般"},"honorifics":[],"selfAddress":[],"specialNames":[],"vip":{"isVIP":0,"from":"0","to":"0"},"marriage":{"aiMarr